# Captured camera responses are byte-exact evidence, not source code.
#
# The simulator serves these verbatim and the tests assert their exact bytes and
# lengths, so line endings must never be rewritten. Without this, cloning on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every LF as CRLF: the /v1/changes payload
# becomes 54 bytes instead of the camera's 53, photos-listing.json gains 29
# stray CRs, and the simulator stops being byte-faithful. CI runs on Linux, so
# nothing would have caught it there.
pyks2/testing/data/** -text
examples/** -text

# Binary captures: no conversion, and no attempt to diff them as text.
*.bin binary
*.jpg binary
